---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SectionPanel from "../components/SectionPanel.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import headshot from "../assets/headshotcompressed.jpg";
---

<Layout title="Jack Yu" description="Portfolio of Jack Yu">
  <div class="content-wrapper">
    <SectionPanel id="about" extraClass="about">
      <h2>About Me</h2>
      <Image
        src={headshot}
        alt="Jack Yu headshot"
        class="image headshot"
        width={180}
        height={180}
        priority
      />

      <p>
        I'm a sophomore studying at Caltech majoring in physics. I am broadly
        interested in developing the robust instrumentation and techniques
        required to realize emerging technological paradigms, including quantum
        sensing, solid-state electrolytes, and nuclear fusion. So far, I have
        worked in Caltech's
        <a href="https://caltechexperimentalgravity.github.io/"
          >Experimental Gravity Group</a
        >, under Professor Rana Adhikari, where I simulate quantum states useful
        for real-world quantum computing and quantum sensing at
        <a href="https://www.ligo.caltech.edu/">LIGO</a>. I also work in the <a
          href="https://cushinglab.caltech.edu/">Cushing Lab</a
        >, where I develop spectroscopic instrumentation and techniques to study
        how ions interact and move in solid-state electrolytes. Before Caltech,
        I spent two summers in an optoelectronics R&D lab at Sandia National
        Labs under Dr. Darwin Serkland and Dr. Alejandro Griñe.
      </p>

      <p>
        Outside the lab, I compete on Caltech's NCAA swim team and enjoy
        printmaking, photography, and reading science fiction.
      </p>

      <p class="bg-credit">
        Background photo: microscope photo of a monolithic Indium Phosphide chip
        developed by Infinera that processes data at 1.6&nbsp;terabits per
        second using light instead of electrons. Colors are inverted from the
        original for aesthetic effect.
      </p>
    </SectionPanel>
  </div>
</Layout>
